# Data conversion between byte and kibibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between byte and kibibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1B to 0.0009KiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5B yields 0.0014KiB; backward, converting 1KiB to 1024B preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5KiB yields 1536.0B.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1B
print(forward_whole->to(KiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(forward_fractional->to(KiB))
backward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(backward_whole->to(B))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(backward_fractional->to(B))

<<< stdout
0.0009KiB
0.0014KiB
1024B
1536.0B

<<< stderr
